.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KAI-RAG 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kai-rag ,
.Nm kai-index
.Nd ask the local assistant a question about this machine, from indexed documentation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm kai-rag
.Ar question ...
.Nm kai-index
.Op Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm kai-rag
sends a question, with the machine's state \(em
.Xr kst 8 ,
unhealthy pools, memory \(em to the local retrieval service on port
8400, which answers from the indexed documentation and streams the reply.
When that service is not running it asks the local model directly,
without the documentation, and says so on standard error.
.Pp
.Nm kai-index
has the retrieval service index a directory of documentation, by default
.Pa /usr/local/share/kldload-ai/html .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when answered or indexed; 1 when the service is not running
.Pq Nm kai-index
or the request failed; 2 for an option
.Nm kai-index
does not know.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kai-index
$ kai-rag 'how do I create a ZFS mirror?'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bobctl 8 ,
.Xr kldload-ai-webui 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: both told the user to run
.Ql kai ,
which nothing installs.
